      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "rw",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 6: give read misses priority over writes. The processor waits for reads; it does not wait for writes."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 6 of 8: reads before writes"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "mlx"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "rw"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Write-through: a read miss arrives while writes sit in the write buffer. The slow way waits for the buffer to drain."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "rw[0][1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The fast way checks the buffer for the address. If it is not there, the read goes to memory at once, ahead of the waiting writes."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "rw[0][2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Write-back: a read miss must evict a dirty block. Instead of writing it back first, copy it to a buffer, read the new block, then write the victim later."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "rw[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Either way, the read's miss penalty no longer includes a write."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "reads are urgent · writes can wait in a buffer"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "vipt",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 7: avoid address translation during indexing. Programs use virtual addresses, but memory uses physical ones, and the TLB translates between them."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 7 of 8: no translation while indexing"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "rw"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "vi"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "A physically indexed cache must wait for the TLB first: translation, then cache. That makes every hit slower."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "vi[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "A fully virtual cache skips the TLB, but two virtual addresses can name the same physical block, the cache must be flushed on a process switch, and protection gets harder."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "vi[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The common answer: virtually indexed, physically tagged. Index the cache with page offset bits, which translation never changes, while the TLB translates the rest in parallel. Then compare physical tags."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "vi[2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "It works only if the index and offset bits fit inside the page offset: cache size over ways must be at most the page size."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "vi"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "vim"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "vim[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "32 kilobytes, 8-way, 4 kilobyte pages: 4 kilobytes per way, so it fits. That is why so many L1 caches are exactly 32 kilobytes and 8-way."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "reveal",
       "target": "vim[1]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "vim[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The same cache 4-way needs 8 kilobytes per way: too big, so it cannot be VIPT."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "reveal",
       "target": "vim[2]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "vim[2]"
      },
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "VIPT: cache size ÷ ways ≤ page size"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
